    "notes": "Served with the darkdatter DGX Spark Qwen3.8-27B recipe (https://github.com/darkdatter/gb10-repo, main 2db1ecd), using its standalone README step 3 path rather than the SparkStation orchestration of step 4: ./scripts/01-build-and-fetch.sh pulled the official LMSYS image lmsysorg/sglang:dev-cu13-qwen38-27b-dflash2 and both pinned checkpoints, then the recipe-pinned MiaAI-Lab toolkit (Qwen3.8-27B-SGLang-DGX-Spark at c90d8c34) launched the server with IMAGE set and DF_EXTRA carrying the recipe tuning. Target RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 at revision 554ebba9, DFlash2 speculative decoding against z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 at revision 50307d4c with 16 draft tokens (the README step 6 interactive optimum), mem-fraction-static 0.85, max-total-tokens capped at 1048576, the README step 5 concurrency trio max-running-requests 16 with max-mamba-cache-size 80 and cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 16, KV cache fp8_e4m3, bf16 mamba SSM state, mamba radix cache extra_buffer, FlashInfer attention with autotune left on, chunked prefill 8192, prefill CUDA graph off, torch.compile off, and the native 262144 context window. The container is CPU-pinned to the GB10 Cortex-X5 cores 5-9,15-19 by the toolkit launcher. The chat template comes from the target repository, reasoning-parser qwen3 and sampling-defaults model, so the served default is thinking on: the speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false, the eval rows use that served default. The server runs without an API key; the harness attached over HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8888 and sent a bearer header the server ignores. No systemd unit, no SparkStation supervisor and no cockpit were installed."
